# Two-span packet ledger

Bounded storage is the discipline of embedded and streaming systems: a ring buffer, a fixed-size cache, a stash that can never grow. When capacity is fixed, every policy — what to evict, when to refuse, how to wrap — is part of the observable behavior.

Represent a wrapped packet by at most two physical spans.

